==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{was wotd|2012|February|7}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|senescere||to grow [[old]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɨnˈɛsəns/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{label|en|biology}} The [[state]] or [[process]] of [[ageing]], especially in [[humans]]; old age.
# {{label|en|cell biology}} Ceasing to divide by [[mitosis]] because of shortening of [[telomere]]s or excessive [[DNA]] damage.
# {{label|en|gerontology}} Old age; accumulated damage to [[macromolecule]]s, [[cell]]s, [[tissue]]s and [[organ]]s with the passage of time.
# {{label|en|botany}} Fruit senescence, leading to ripening of fruit.

